# The scaling by a of a ball with one-limb center, with the special states of a ball:
# ball_scale_1, then the fix-up of milestone1.md, "Ball kernels".
# One ball operand, so q is rx itself; |cz0| is named az here, since a is the operand.
kernel:        ball_scale_1_full
input:         stored cx
input:         stored rx
input:         a
output:        cw
output:        rw
value:         cx*a
requires:      ball cx rx
ensures:       encloses cw rw x*a x=cx,rx
min_precision: 2
source:        ball_scale_1, then the fix-up of the special states of a ball (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       core: as ball_scale_1; fix-up: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the fix-up selects, after explicit tests that the center and the radius are finite (f) and that no operand is empty (e); B1 to B4 of milestone1.md, "Ball kernels", state what comes out

(cz, rz) = ball_scale_1(cx, rx, a)
e        = eq(rx, rx)
az       = abs(cz)
f1       = lt(az, const inf)
f2       = lt(rz, const inf)
f        = and(f1, f2)
c0       = select(f, cz, 0)
r        = select(f, rz, const inf)
cw       = select(e, c0, rx)
rw       = select(e, r, rx)
